message.content:
{
 "summary": "This bill would expand the rules for school library collections to include classroom libraries. It defines a classroom library as materials acquired by a teacher and made available to their students. Materials include items such as books, films, video games, and subscription content. Local boards of education and public charter school governing bodies would be required to adopt policies for developing and reviewing both school library collections and classroom libraries.\n\nThese policies must include a procedure for teachers, parents, and legal guardians to review and refer classroom library materials for evaluation. They must also provide parents and legal guardians multiple opportunities each school year to view the books in their student's classroom libraries. Additionally, the policies must prohibit teachers from intentionally bypassing library collection policies using their classroom libraries, such as by including materials deemed inappropriate for students' age and maturity levels or unsuitable for the school's educational mission. The bill also amends existing law to ensure that procedures for referring and removing materials apply to classroom libraries as well as school library collections. This act would take effect upon becoming law."
}
